1	# MCP Time Server
2	
3	This is the MCP (Model Context Protocol) Time Server, extracted from the official [modelcontextprotocol/servers](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers) repository.
4	
5	## Source
6	
7	This server was originally located at:
8	- Repository: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers
9	- Path: `/src/time`
10	- Original commit: Extracted from the main branch
11	
12	## Description
13	
14	A Model Context Protocol server that provides time and timezone functionality. This server enables LLMs to get current time information across different timezones.
15	
16	## Features
17	
18	- Get current time in any timezone
19	- List available timezones
20	- Convert times between timezones
21	
22	## Installation
23	
24	```bash
25	# Using pip
26	pip install -e .
27	
28	# Using uv
29	uv pip install -e .
30	```
31	
32	## Usage
33	
34	The server can be used with any MCP-compatible client.
35	
36	## License
37	
38	This project maintains the same license as the original modelcontextprotocol/servers repository.
39	
40	## Acknowledgments
41	
42	All credit goes to the original authors at Anthropic and contributors to the modelcontextprotocol/servers project.

